{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1499273-matter-2-prime-2-what-material-would-you-conjure-to-make-money","id":1499273,"title":"Matter 2 + Prime 2 - what material would you conjure to make money?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-12-10T03:12:53-08:00","id":1499273,"title":"Matter 2 + Prime 2 - what material would you conjure to make money?","content":"The obvious, tropey thing is creating gold. Wonderful. Expensive, if you have good Crafts you can create it as rings or even necklaces, sell them... But it would be noticed pretty quickly. At best you're a suspected thief. At worst, the Union is getting involved.<br /> <br /> Then I think of less obvious things. Creating big bundles of copper wiring, likely stripped from walls. Good quality candlewax. Valuable inks.<br /> <br /> Criteria for an ideal conjuring material:<br /> <br /> - simple enough to make with Prime 2 + Matter 2<br /> - simple enough not to require insane investment in abilities to understand how to create it ex nihilo<br /> - valuable<br /> - little regulation or oversight<br /> - you can explain bringing the material in to sell regularly<br /> <br /> Any good candidates?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-10T09:05:55-08:00","id":1499282,"title":"","content":"Gold is by far the simplest. Conjure some gold rings or chains and sell to a pawn shop. <br /> <br /> If you have more sophisticated connections certain rare minerals are more expensive than gold. With the right connections there's plenty of profit.<br /> <br /> A subtler way of acting might be to build a set of contacts in the memorabilia trades and the sellers of collectibles. Showing up every now and then with some old collectibles. Comic books, paperbacks of cult authors, movie lobby cards and posters, toys, or baseball cards, stay away from the super rare stuff and you'd have a paradox free living at hand. <br /> <br /> Cleaning out storage lockers and haunting yard sales can make it all coincidental.<br /> <br /> Pretend to be a prospector (enjoying hiking helps) pretend to be looking for crystals. Conjure up large fine but nonspectacular stones. Enough to live comfortably on, but not to raise suspicion. <br /> <br /> Change your scam regularly to avoid attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 12-10-2022, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-10T09:34:04-08:00","id":1499288,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'd just take advantage of the fact that one interpretation of the Prime Sphere is that it's the \u201cmoney Sphere\u201d. I wouldn't worry about what form the money takes; just use a Prime 2 Effect to gain access to a temporary Resources Background at the cost of one Quintessence per dot. (This is an inversion of the concept of Primal Ventures, which require you to invest a dot of Resources into a Venture for every point of Quintessence it can generate.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-10-2022, 12:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-10T11:33:39-08:00","id":1499299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1499273-matter-2-prime-2-what-material-would-you-conjure-to-make-money?p=1499282#post1499282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gold is by far the simplest. Conjure some gold rings or chains and sell to a pawn shop.<br /> <br /> If you have more sophisticated connections certain rare minerals are more expensive than gold. With the right connections there's plenty of profit.<br /> <br /> A subtler way of acting might be to build a set of contacts in the memorabilia trades and the sellers of collectibles. Showing up every now and then with some old collectibles. Comic books, paperbacks of cult authors, movie lobby cards and posters, toys, or baseball cards, stay away from the super rare stuff and you'd have a paradox free living at hand.<br /> <br /> Cleaning out storage lockers and haunting yard sales can make it all coincidental.<br /> <br /> Pretend to be a prospector (enjoying hiking helps) pretend to be looking for crystals. Conjure up large fine but nonspectacular stones. Enough to live comfortably on, but not to raise suspicion.<br /> <br /> Change your scam regularly to avoid attention.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah changing what you're doing regularly seems to be very key.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-10T13:58:43-08:00","id":1499312,"title":"","content":"Is selling the conjured material directly a requirement?<br /> <br /> If not, create something consumable as an energy source, and sell the energy into the grid (obviously local laws may influence this). Decentralized power is a big part of most plans to resolve the climate crisis, so the Union isn't going to be too worried about some farmer in the middle of nowhere that's converted a bunch of acreage into renewable energy production enough to make it a regular source of income.<br /> <br /> This also mix's fairly well with Dataweaver's points about Prime (or Primal Utility) as the &quot;money&quot; Sphere as it were.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-10T17:18:46-08:00","id":1499324,"title":"","content":"Prime and Forces could create a nice little power source. <br /> <br /> Prime and Matter might keep something like an old grist mill running with minimal maintenance to generate power. A side hustle that provides a living for a couple of hours of effort each month would be a very useful thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-11T04:48:21-08:00","id":1499360,"title":"","content":"Just Life 2 and grow pot.<br /> <br /> Jokes aside, the one quick money grab is obviously Entropy 1/2 at a cassino. Just dont over reach in Vegas, or you'll end up strapped into a chair taking a beat by an Enforcer.<br /> <br /> Take that money, put it into a bank, and Entropy 1 your way into the &quot;Day Trading&quot; market of speculative assets.<br /> <br /> Do it for a while, and make sure not to exaggerate again, buy a piece of land and Life 3 all your cows for them to be super healthy, eat as little as possible and produce incridible amounts of milk.<br /> <br /> Life 2 your wheat, apple threes, strawberries bushes, whatever you decide to produce.<br /> <br /> Search out for buyers, offer them good discounts, hire a good accountant, enjoy the fruits of your hard labor and your new status as &quot;community pillar&quot;.<br /> <br /> Now, Mind 2 around the tiny town close to your farm for some time, making the folks there become drawn to you, until you can finally open up your own personal cult. Have them sell their lands to you at a discount, and now you own the city and the inhabitants are your acolytes and labor force.<br /> <br /> You see, this is why we in the Union have to hunt your Mage's predatory asses down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-11T07:28:46-08:00","id":1499369,"title":"","content":"The proper use of Mind 2/Prime 2 is to create the illusion that your Chantry is something respectable but brutally dull. So no one can be bothered to pay attention to what you do. <br /> <br /> Then use the Life magic to grow the most exquisite plants. Sell said plants to a &quot;Farm to Table&quot; restaurant or a group of them. <br /> <br /> If cannabis is legal in your state, excellent weed is a path to quicker profits.<br /> <br /> Hurting people always brings in too much attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-11T17:45:32-08:00","id":1499412,"title":"","content":"Really, the best way to make money as a mage is as a speculator with Entropy 1 in small doses (no turning millionaire over the night, or you'll end up in a room 101 before the end of the month) or Life 2 and a farm.<br /> <br /> No matter the case, you always have to take care not to over do, otherwise you'll get too much attention (just imagine every agronomy institute wanting to know your &quot;secrets&quot; for having such massive production over such a small tile of land).<br /> <br /> In the end, if you want to survive in the WoD, the best to do is to have small and constant increments, so &quot;easy money&quot; wont ever be the answer, but rather &quot;hard&quot; work and patience, those two qualities can help a fledgling Mage build up an empire.<br /> <br /> Also, I recommend always using Entropy 1 regardless, unless you already have good levels on Accounting, because you'll need to cover the basis for your businesses - how can you have prices so bellow the market? How can you have such a high productivity? If those numbers start to get too much attention, you'll have problems sooner or later, so throw in Entropy 1 to &quot;guess&quot; which prices to practice and remain competitive but without having the government start thinking that you may be a laundring scheme for some criminal front, nor having such a high productivity that magazines take notice and start trying to get an interview with you to understand your &quot;secret&quot;. So Entropy 1 is for keeping your feet in the ground and doing good without being fantastic - preferably even, just slightly above the average, which is what you'll do if you're smart. Entropy 1 will also help you keep your profits &quot;random&quot;, instead of just win after win after win, which would be super suspicious for those that keep an active eye on that type of stuff (you know who I refer to), which includes even losing sometimes on purpose for the sake of keeping the facade.<br /> <br /> This means a pretty conservative and modest business growth, but a constant and reliable one, which is worth far more than crazy gambles that may end up with the FBI - or worse, the Men in Black - knocking on your doorsteps.<br /> <br /> Other spheres are still pretty useful of course, you will still be using Life 2 to grow your wheat, but Entropy 1 will tell you when enough is enough. And you can keep 2 books for your cash flux, and use that money from the &quot;parallel&quot; market to buy, lets call it, &quot;exotic&quot; items (like smuggled fauna and flora, strange crystals from the Himalayans or supercomputers), without drawing too much attention.<br /> <br /> Here, Entropy 1 helps too in order to find new contacts - which group of pirate smugglers are reliable and trustworthy enough to work with.<br /> <br /> So, maybe it is not advisable to produce 100 tons of wheat in a single acre of land, at least not for the IRS to know, but perhaps you know a crew of sailors that smuggle it to North Korea, pay in gold and dont make questions, and you know just the guys that smuggle computers from China and Russia and accept gold as payment...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}